# dsk_talk: the TEROPOLY TABLE TALK reads as sentences (2026-11-09, owner: "make the table talk readable"). The right pane of the editor (title `TEROPOLY table talk`) used to print the raw ledger result text
# (`r5 p2 roll to=13;for-sale`, `r5 p2 buy bought-140`, `r6 p1 offer id=5;give=prop:26;get=cash:900;round=1`, `card=luck:15`). Now ONE function of the engine (`talk_row` in @.apps/deskopoly/ops/deskopoly.c) turns a replayed ledger row into a
# short sentence with the player NAMES (join rows) and the tile LABELS and deck names (page.pdl LABEL rows) and the card's own wording (cards.pdl): `B bought Phi Lane for $140`, `A offered B: Coil Plaza for $30 (offer #5)`.
# It is published as the additive feed keys `logt_<k>` (next to the unchanged raw `log_<k>`); the driver shows `logt_` and falls back to `log_` for an empty one; the verb `talk [--out <file> | --row "<EVENT row>"]` prints the same sentences for a harness.
# THE LEDGER IS NEVER CHANGED: the pinned ledger hash of the seed-6 game (72442143905f2371, case dsk_pettrade) is asserted again AFTER talk and ui have run.
# Method: sentences are checked three ways. (1) SWEEPS: three whole games (the 831-row seed-6 pets game, the 840-row pet_trades game, the engine-made 47-row fixture of dsk_tradeui) and the 68-row fixture of the live game
#   (amend, cancel, counter, reject) are turned into sentences with `talk --out`; the file must hold one line per ledger row, no row falls back to raw text (raw=0), no line contains a raw token (to= id= give= get= card= bought- ;)
#   - and the same grep is run on the RAW ledger as the positive control - and for every verb the number of sentences of its shape equals the number of ledger rows of that verb (a counter computed by grep on both sides). (2) ONE ROW PER KIND:
#   every row kind the engine writes (lobby join leave start order first seat roll jail_roll jail_pay jail_card buy skip bid pass auction_end end_turn bankrupt pay_debt build sell mortgage unmortgage offer counter amend accept reject cancel expire
#   over, and every roll token) as a hand-written `--row` with its exact sentence. (3) THE PANE: `ui` publishes logt_0..7 (pinned exactly) and the REAL driver publishes them as the chat rows gml_*.
# NEGATIVES: an unknown kind comes back as the old raw text (known=0, and a sweep with such a row reports raw=1); a wrong name fails (`A bought` is absent where B bought); a renamed tile label changes the sentence (labels are data); a changed card
#   wording changes the sentence (card text is data); names come from the join rows (Ava Ben Cy); the grep for raw tokens is shown to match the raw ledger (it CAN fail).
# NOT COVERED: how the window wraps the pane (open the PNG: about 24 characters per line), the mini ruleset (its own ui), the driver's fallback to log_ for an engine without logt_ (checked by hand against an engine built from git HEAD, see the compendium).
RESULTS | ../results/dsk_talk.txt
ENV | LC_ALL | C

CASE    | setup
SCRATCH |
COPYDIR | @.apps/deskopoly | app | ops,deskopoly-pchq,state
MKDIR   | m
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | lobby | classic
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | join | A | pet
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | join | B | pet
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | join | C | pet
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | start | 6
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | autoplay
EXPECT_OUT | AUTOPLAY events=831 rounds=94 over=1 winner=p3 | the-base-game-is-the-seed-6-pets-game-of-dsk_pettrade
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | ledger_hash
EXPECT_OUT | rows=831 hash=72442143905f2371 | the-ledger-hash-before-any-talk


CASE    | sweep6
RUN | $HOUSE/@.apps/deskopoly/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/m | talk | --out | $T/m.out
EXPECT_OUT_IS | TALK rows=831 raw=0 | EVERY-ONE-OF-THE-831-ROWS-HAS-A-SENTENCE-and-none-fell-back-to-raw-text
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -c | ^ | $T/m.out
EXPECT_OUT_IS | 831 | the-sentence-file-has-one-line-per-ledger-row
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -c | ^$ | $T/m.out
EXPECT_OUT_IS | 0 | and-no-sentence-is-empty
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -c | -E | to=\pid=\pgive=\pget=\pcard=\pbought-\p; | $T/m.out
EXPECT_OUT_IS | 0 | NO-SENTENCE-CONTAINS-A-RAW-TOKEN-to=-id=-give=-get=-card=-bought--or-a-semicolon
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -c | -E | to=\pbought-\pcard=\p; | $T/m/ledger.txt
CAPTURE | rawleaks
EXPECT_GE | $rawleaks | 600 | POSITIVE-CONTROL-the-same-grep-on-the-RAW-ledger-finds-the-tokens-in-hundreds-of-rows-so-the-zero-above-CAN-fail
